PORTFOLIO DASHBOARD — TEKNISK LOGIKSPEC V1

PORTFOLIO DASHBOARD — TEKNISK LOGIKSPEC V1
Status: första tekniska logikspec för implementation av Portfolio Dashboard
Syfte: översätta master-spec V1 till deterministiska regler för viktstatus, trendstatus, riskstatus, hedge-status, dry powder-status och graceful degradation
Princip: hellre enkel, förklarbar och robust V1-logik än överoptimerad pseudoexakt modell
Arkitekturprincip: denna logikspec får använda portfolio admin-data, portföljvikter, prisserier, macro regime och sector regime som inputs, men får inte skriva tillbaka till andra lager

====================================================
0. INPUTS OCH GRUNDDEFINITIONER
====================================================

Obligatoriska input-objekt i V1:

A. Portfolio admin metadata
Per portfölj:
- portfolioId
- portfolioType
- active
- includedInTotalPortfolio
- targetWeightPct
- minWeightPct
- maxWeightPct
- strategicRiskLevel
- hedgingAllowed
- allowedHedgeTypes[]
- maxHedgePct
- hedgePurpose[]
- rebalanceMode
- maxSinglePositionPct optional
- maxSectorConcentrationPct optional
- maxCommodityConcentrationPct optional
- maxJuniorExposurePct optional
- maxIlliquidExposurePct optional

B. Portfolio weights / values
Per portfölj:
- currentMarketValue
- actualWeightPct

C. Historical performance / price series
Per portfölj:
- daily total return index OR daily market value history
Minimum recommended for full trend signal:
- 200 trading days history

D. Optional but preferred position breakdown
Per portfölj:
- holdings[]
- position weights
- sector tags
- commodity tags
- liquidity flags
- junior/pre-revenue flags

E. Macro / Sector inputs
- macroRegime optional
- sectorRegime per relevant portfolio optional

F. Cash / dry powder inputs
- opportunistic portfolio current weight if included
- or explicit cash allocation if modeled within opportunistic

====================================================
1. GLOBALA DOMÄNREGLER
====================================================

1.1 Only active portfolios may receive operational status
- if active = false → portfolio excluded from status calculations

1.2 Only includedInTotalPortfolio = true count toward total allocation logic
- portfolios visible in UI but not included in total shall not affect total weights

1.3 Missing values
- null or non-finite values must never silently generate “healthy” signal
- missing data must degrade signal to partial or unavailable

1.4 Classification precedence
When multiple negative conditions apply, the more severe status wins.

Example:
critical_overweight overrides overweight
hedge_urgent overrides hedge_recommended
critical risk overrides elevated risk

====================================================
2. VALIDATION-REGLER
====================================================

2.1 Target weight sum validation
Compute:
SUM(targetWeightPct) across portfolios where:
- active = true
- includedInTotalPortfolio = true

Rules:
- if sum = 100.0 exactly or within tolerance ±0.10 pp → valid
- if abs(sum - 100.0) > 0.10 pp and <= 1.00 pp → warning
- if abs(sum - 100.0) > 1.00 pp → error

Recommended output:
- weightPlanValidationStatus:
  - valid
  - warning
  - error

2.2 Individual band validation
Per included active portfolio:
- minWeightPct must be <= targetWeightPct
- targetWeightPct must be <= maxWeightPct
- if violated → admin validation error

2.3 Negative or absurd values
- target/min/max weights < 0 not allowed
- maxWeightPct > 100 not allowed
- actualWeightPct < 0 not allowed

====================================================
3. WEIGHTSTATUS-LOGIK
====================================================

Definitioner:
- bandWidthPct = maxWeightPct - minWeightPct
- distanceToNearestBandEdgePct = min(
    abs(actualWeightPct - minWeightPct),
    abs(maxWeightPct - actualWeightPct)
  )

Prerequisite:
- actualWeightPct, minWeightPct, maxWeightPct must be available

If prerequisites missing:
- weightStatus = unavailable
- rebalanceStatus = unavailable

3.1 Core band states
- if actualWeightPct < minWeightPct → underweight
- if actualWeightPct > maxWeightPct → overweight
- if minWeightPct <= actualWeightPct <= maxWeightPct → candidate within_band/watch

3.2 Watch rule
Within band, portfolio becomes watch if near either edge.

V1 watch threshold:
- watch if distanceToNearestBandEdgePct <= max(1.0 pp, 0.25 * bandWidthPct)

Otherwise:
- within_band

3.3 Critical band break rule
Under/overweight becomes critical if break exceeds threshold.

Define:
- lowerBreakPct = minWeightPct - actualWeightPct
- upperBreakPct = actualWeightPct - maxWeightPct

V1 critical threshold:
- critical if break > max(2.0 pp, 0.33 * bandWidthPct)

Thus:
- if actualWeightPct < minWeightPct:
    - if lowerBreakPct > criticalThreshold → critical_underweight
    - else → underweight

- if actualWeightPct > maxWeightPct:
    - if upperBreakPct > criticalThreshold → critical_overweight
    - else → overweight

3.4 WeightStatus enum
Allowed outputs:
- within_band
- watch
- underweight
- overweight
- critical_underweight
- critical_overweight
- unavailable

====================================================
4. REBALANCESTATUS-LOGIK
====================================================

rebalancing should be driven primarily by weightStatus,
secondarily by rebalanceMode,
optionally by trend/risk overlays later.

4.1 Base mapping from weightStatus
- within_band → no_action
- watch → monitor
- underweight → rebalance_soon
- overweight → rebalance_soon
- critical_underweight → rebalance_now
- critical_overweight → rebalance_now
- unavailable → unavailable

4.2 rebalanceMode modifier
If rebalanceMode = soft:
- watch stays monitor
- under/overweight stays rebalance_soon
- critical stays rebalance_now

If rebalanceMode = standard:
- same as base mapping

If rebalanceMode = strict:
- watch escalates from monitor → rebalance_soon
- under/overweight stays rebalance_soon
- critical stays rebalance_now

4.3 Optional future overlay
Risk/trend may later influence urgency, but not in V1 core unless explicitly added.

Allowed outputs:
- no_action
- monitor
- rebalance_soon
- rebalance_now
- unavailable

====================================================
5. TRENDSTATUS-LOGIK
====================================================

Trend signal must be deterministic but simple in V1.

5.1 Required daily history for full trend signal
Need at least:
- 200 trading days history for full short/medium/long model

If available history:
- >= 200 days → full
- >= 65 and < 200 → partial
- < 65 → unavailable

5.2 V1 trend horizons
Use fixed lookbacks for V1:
- short trend = 20 trading days
- medium trend = 65 trading days
- long trend = 200 trading days

5.3 Trend measures
For each available horizon H:
- return_H = total return over lookback H

Direction per horizon:
- positive if return_H > +2.0%
- negative if return_H < -2.0%
- neutral otherwise

Threshold rationale:
- avoids noise around zero in portfolio-level signals

5.4 Relative strength
If at least 2 active included portfolios have valid same-horizon return data:
- compute percentile rank of each portfolio by medium-term return (65d)
- top 30% = strong relative
- bottom 30% = weak relative
- otherwise neutral relative

If insufficient comparable portfolios:
- relative strength unavailable, do not block core trendStatus

5.5 Core trendStatus classification
Use available horizons with preference to longer trend.

A. strong_uptrend
- long positive
- medium positive
- short positive or neutral

B. improving
- medium positive
- short positive
- long neutral or unavailable or modestly negative

C. neutral
- mixed signals without clear deterioration or improvement
- OR all available horizons neutral

D. weakening
- medium negative
- short negative
- long neutral or unavailable

E. downtrend
- long negative
- medium negative
- short negative or neutral

Fallback partial logic:
If only short+medium available:
- strong_uptrend if both positive
- downtrend if both negative
- improving if short positive and medium neutral/positive
- weakening if short negative and medium neutral/negative
- else neutral

If only medium available:
- positive → improving
- negative → weakening
- neutral → neutral

5.6 trendStatus outputs
- strong_uptrend
- improving
- neutral
- weakening
- downtrend
- unavailable

5.7 Supporting trend diagnostics
Recommended debug fields:
- return_20d
- return_65d
- return_200d
- shortDirection
- mediumDirection
- longDirection
- relativeStrengthBucket optional

====================================================
6. MOMENTUM/BREDD — V1 REGLER
====================================================

V1 should keep internal breadth optional, not blocking.

6.1 Internal breadth applicability
If holdings data exists and portfolio has >= 5 holdings:
- breadth may be computed
Else:
- breadth unavailable

6.2 Simple breadth definition
- breadthPct = % of holdings with positive 65d return

Interpretation:
- broad_strength if breadthPct >= 65%
- broad_weakness if breadthPct <= 35%
- mixed otherwise

6.3 V1 usage
Breadth is supporting information only in V1.
It should not override trendStatus.
It may be shown in debug or supplementary UI if available.

====================================================
7. RISKSTATUS-LOGIK
====================================================

RiskStatus in V1 should be score-based and explainable.
Use 4 components where possible:
- volatility
- drawdown
- concentration
- cyclicality/speculation

If some components missing, degrade gracefully.

7.1 Scoring scale per component
Each component gets score:
- 0 = calm
- 1 = elevated
- 2 = high
- 3 = critical

Total score:
riskScore = average of available component scores

Map average score to riskStatus:
- < 0.75 → calm
- >= 0.75 and < 1.50 → elevated
- >= 1.50 and < 2.25 → high
- >= 2.25 → critical

Minimum requirement:
- at least 2 components available for full riskStatus
- if only 1 component available → partial riskStatus
- if 0 components available → unavailable

----------------------------------------------------
7.2 Volatility component
Prerequisite:
- at least 65 trading days of return history

Metric:
- annualized volatility from last 65 daily returns

Thresholds:
- vol < 15% → score 0
- 15% to < 25% → score 1
- 25% to < 40% → score 2
- >= 40% → score 3

----------------------------------------------------
7.3 Drawdown component
Prerequisite:
- at least 200 trading days preferred, 65 minimum partial

Metric:
- current drawdown from trailing 200d peak
If 200d not available but 65d available:
- use trailing available peak and flag partial

Thresholds:
- drawdown < 8% → score 0
- 8% to < 15% → score 1
- 15% to < 25% → score 2
- >= 25% → score 3

----------------------------------------------------
7.4 Concentration component
Use holdings data if available.

Primary metric:
- top holding weight

Secondary optional metric:
- sum of top 3 holdings

Thresholds using top holding:
- top holding < 12% → score 0
- 12% to < 20% → score 1
- 20% to < 30% → score 2
- >= 30% → score 3

If holdings unavailable:
- component unavailable

----------------------------------------------------
7.5 Cyclicality / speculation component
This is portfolio-type-aware.

Base scores by portfolioType:
- stable_income → 0
- growth → 1
- commodity_majors → 1
- commodity_junior → 2
- opportunistic → 0

Escalation rules if data available:
- if commodity_junior actualWeightPct > targetWeightPct and trendStatus = downtrend → +1 score cap at 3
- if opportunistic weight very low relative to total risk and total risk high/critical → this affects dry powder, not this component directly
- if holdings data shows junior/pre-revenue exposure within non-junior portfolio above allowed policy → +1 score cap at 3

If no extra data:
- use base score

----------------------------------------------------
7.6 Strategic risk cross-check
Strategic risk does not set actual riskStatus directly,
but can generate mismatch flag.

Map strategicRiskLevel to expected max normal score:
- low → expected <= 1
- medium → expected <= 1.5
- high → expected <= 2
- extreme → expected <= 3

If actual riskScore materially exceeds strategic expectation by >0.75:
- set riskMismatchFlag = true

7.7 riskStatus outputs
- calm
- elevated
- high
- critical
- unavailable

====================================================
8. TOTAL PORTFOLIO RISKSTATUS
====================================================

Total portfolio risk should be computed separately from per-portfolio risk.

8.1 Inputs
Use included active portfolios only.

8.2 Weighted portfolio risk score
- totalRiskScore = weighted average of per-portfolio riskScore
  weighted by actualWeightPct

8.3 Escalation conditions
Escalate total risk by +0.25 score equivalent if any of:
- commodity_junior actualWeightPct > its maxWeightPct
- top single portfolio actualWeightPct > 55% of total
- 2 or more risky portfolios (riskStatus high/critical) together exceed 50%
- dry powder insufficient while total risk already high/critical

Then remap to status thresholds from section 7.1.

8.4 Outputs
- calm
- elevated
- high
- critical
- unavailable

====================================================
9. HEDGESTATUS-LOGIK
====================================================

Hedge signal in V1 is recommendation logic, not execution logic.

9.1 Inputs
Per portfolio:
- riskStatus
- trendStatus
- hedgingAllowed
- allowedHedgeTypes[]
- hedgePurpose[]
- actualWeightPct vs band
- optional macroRegime
- optional sectorRegime

9.2 Base hedge need score per portfolio
Start at 0 and add:

A. Risk contribution
- riskStatus calm → +0
- elevated → +1
- high → +2
- critical → +3

B. Trend contribution
- strong_uptrend → +0
- improving → +0
- neutral → +1
- weakening → +2
- downtrend → +3

C. Weight stress contribution
- within_band → +0
- watch → +0
- under/overweight → +1
- critical under/overweight → +2

D. Macro/sector overlay contribution (if available)
Suggested V1 mapping:
- if macroRegime indicates broad risk-off / contraction / stress → +1
- if relevant sectorRegime deteriorating for that portfolio → +1

Max base score not capped until mapping stage.

9.3 Hedge need mapping
Per portfolio:
- score 0–2 → hedge_not_needed
- score 3–4 → consider_hedge
- score 5–6 → hedge_recommended
- score >= 7 → hedge_urgent

9.4 Policy filter
If hedgingAllowed = true and allowedHedgeTypes non-empty:
- keep hedgeStatus as above
- recommended hedge type must come from allowed list

If hedgingAllowed = false OR no allowed direct hedge types:
- convert status to fallback defensive action:
  - consider_hedge → reduce_exposure
  - hedge_recommended → rebalance_to_cash
  - hedge_urgent → increase_dry_powder OR rotate_to_defensive_bucket
- never emit direct hedge recommendation in violation of policy

9.5 Hedge type suggestion hierarchy
If direct hedge allowed, suggested type may follow purpose:

For general market drawdown:
- prefer index_put
- else index_short
- else inverse_etf
- else cash

For inflation / monetary stress:
- prefer gold
- else commodity-linked hedge if policy allows
- else cash

For USD strength:
- prefer usd

For commodity-specific downturn:
- prefer commodity_put
- else producer_pair_hedge
- else reduce exposure

If multiple allowed, prefer lowest-complexity liquid hedge:
index_put > inverse_etf > index_short is debatable in practice,
but V1 recommendation:
- prefer simplest liquid implementable allowed instrument
Exact order can be implementation-configurable.

9.6 Hedge outputs
Direct outputs:
- hedge_not_needed
- consider_hedge
- hedge_recommended
- hedge_urgent

Fallback policy-bound outputs:
- reduce_exposure
- rebalance_to_cash
- increase_dry_powder
- rotate_to_defensive_bucket

9.7 Total hedge signal
Compute from included active portfolios.

Method:
- choose highest severity across portfolios, weighted by actualWeightPct
- practical rule:
  - if any portfolio >20% weight has hedge_urgent → total = hedge_urgent
  - else if weighted average hedge need score >= 5 → total = hedge_recommended
  - else if weighted average hedge need score >= 3 → total = consider_hedge
  - else → hedge_not_needed

Policy conflict rule:
- total signal may not override per-portfolio policy
- if total hedge needed but no meaningful direct hedge permitted anywhere:
  emit total fallback:
  - increase_dry_powder
  - rebalance_to_defensive_bucket

====================================================
10. DRY POWDER STATUS-LOGIK
====================================================

Dry powder in V1 should be tied to opportunistic allocation and total risk environment.

10.1 Inputs
- opportunistic actualWeightPct if active and included
- totalPortfolio riskStatus
- optional cash value if modeled separately inside opportunistic

10.2 Required minimum dry powder by risk environment
V1 baseline thresholds:
- total risk calm → minimum 5%
- elevated → minimum 8%
- high → minimum 12%
- critical → minimum 15%

These are intentionally moderate V1 defaults, not eternal truths.

10.3 Classification
Let DP = opportunistic actualWeightPct

For current total risk environment minimum = M

- if DP < M → insufficient_dry_powder
- if DP >= M and DP < M + 5 pp → adequate_dry_powder
- if DP >= M + 5 pp and DP < M + 12 pp → deployable_cash_available
- if DP >= M + 12 pp → elevated_cash_buffer

If opportunistic portfolio absent or not included and no explicit cash proxy:
- dryPowderStatus = unavailable

10.4 Total override interaction
If total hedge fallback requires increase_dry_powder:
- and dryPowderStatus = insufficient_dry_powder
  confirm strong defensive signal

====================================================
11. TOTAL SIGNALS — AGGREGATION
====================================================

The overview should produce top-level signals.

11.1 Allocation plan status
- if all included active portfolios within_band or watch → within_allocation_plan
- if any overweight/underweight → outside_allocation_plan
- if any critical band break → materially_outside_allocation_plan

11.2 Drawdown concentration
If position data by portfolio values available:
- identify contribution to total drawdown by portfolio

V1 simple rule:
- if one portfolio contributes >50% of total portfolio drawdown over 65d window
  → drawdown_concentration = true

If unavailable:
- drawdown_concentration = unavailable

11.3 Excessive junior/speculative exposure
V1 simple rule:
- if commodity_junior actualWeightPct > maxWeightPct
  OR
  if commodity_junior actualWeightPct > 15% of total
  → excessive_junior_exposure = true

Else false

11.4 Excessive commodity cyclicality
V1 simple rule:
- commodity exposure = commodity_majors + commodity_junior actual weights
- if combined commodity exposure > 40% AND total risk high/critical
  → excessive_commodity_cyclicality = true
Else false

This is a diagnostic signal only, not an allocation constraint.

====================================================
12. GRACEFUL DEGRADATION — DETERMINISTISK V1
====================================================

Each signal family should have explicit dependency minimums.

12.1 WeightStatus / RebalanceStatus
Requires:
- actualWeightPct
- minWeightPct
- maxWeightPct
If any missing → unavailable

12.2 TrendStatus
- full requires >= 200d history
- partial requires >= 65d history
- unavailable if < 65d

12.3 RiskStatus
- full requires at least 2 valid components
- partial if exactly 1 component valid
- unavailable if 0 components valid

If partial:
- status may still be shown but flagged partial
- severity should not be auto-escalated only because of missing data

12.4 HedgeStatus
Requires minimum:
- riskStatus not unavailable
- trendStatus not unavailable
- hedge policy fields present

If macro/sector unavailable:
- hedge may still be computed without overlay
- mark as partial if overlay absent

If risk or trend unavailable:
- hedgeStatus = insufficient_data_for_hedge_signal

12.5 DryPowderStatus
Requires:
- opportunistic actualWeightPct or equivalent cash proxy
- total riskStatus

If total risk unavailable but opportunistic weight available:
- use calm baseline minimum and flag partial

If both missing:
- unavailable

